sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-08> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Unlike mobile automata or Turing machines, substitution systems cannot in general be emulated one step per cellular automaton step, because the number of elements in a substitution system can be multiplied by a factor each step while a cellular automaton pattern can grow only by a fixed amount per step; progressively more cellular automaton steps are needed per substitution step.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cellular automata cannot emulate substitution systems step for step";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “Emulating Other Systems with Cellular Automata” (from p. 656), p. 658. Scope: cellular automaton emulation of substitution systems"
}
